# Attachment

Name the document in the link, then give its format, size and language when you know them. Someone choosing between a PDF manual and an HTML page needs those details before they select. Prefer an HTML version when the content works as a page. File wording is owned by [Attachments](../../content/formatting-content/attachments.html).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use it for household manuals, installation instructions and maintenance documents. For example, write “Heat pump manual (PDF, 2MB)” rather than “Download”. A thumbnail is optional and must not add a second keyboard stop for the same download.

## Structure and behaviour

Give each entry a meaningful title and a real destination. Add file type, measured size and revision only when known. Keep document information separate from live appliance state. A link that opens a manual and a button that changes an appliance do different jobs, so keep them apart.

## Home Assistant boundary

This reference does not create a document store, request an accessible copy or download a file. The examples open an in-page text preview. Do not show an accessible-format request link unless someone is responsible for fulfilling it. Check permission before publishing manufacturer artwork.

